From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wig Cheng <onlywig@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:43:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: ethernet: w6300: wait for TX free space before
 writing

w6300_tx() resets tx_sem and takes it after issuing SEND to wait for
SENDOK. If the interrupt thread processes the previous send's SENDOK
between the reset and the take, the take completes for the wrong send:
the next w6300_tx() call then rewrites the TX buffer and issues SEND
while the chip is still transmitting, corrupting its TX state. Once
that happens the chip never raises SENDOK again and all transmission
(including ARP replies) stops until a power cycle.

The 10 ms tx_sem timeout widens the window: the frame was already
committed with SEND, so its late SENDOK becomes a stale credit for
the next call.

Poll Sn_TX_FSR until the chip reports enough free space before
touching the TX buffer, using chip state as the ground truth for send
completion. The sibling eth_w5500 driver avoids the overlap through
credit semantics (tx_sem initialized to 1 and never reset); gating on
the FSR also covers the semaphore-timeout path.

Observed on W6300-EVB-Pico2 (RP2350): a sustained TCP upload made the
board drop off the network within seconds to minutes; with this change
it survives.

Signed-off-by: Wig Cheng <onlywig@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c b/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c
index 337d5577da2..43cc11f3b01 100644
--- a/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c
+++ b/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c
@@ -225,6 +225,7 @@ static int w6300_tx(const struct device *dev, struct net_pkt *pkt)
 {
 	struct w6300_runtime *ctx = dev->data;
 	uint16_t len = (uint16_t)net_pkt_get_len(pkt);
+	k_timepoint_t end = sys_timepoint_calc(K_MSEC(W6300_CMD_TIMEOUT_MS));
 	uint16_t offset;
 	uint8_t tmp[2];
 	int ret;
@@ -235,6 +236,24 @@ static int w6300_tx(const struct device *dev, struct net_pkt *pkt)
 
 	k_sem_reset(&ctx->tx_sem);
 
+	while (true) {
+		ret = w6300_spi_read(dev, W6300_BSB_SOCK(0), W6300_Sn_TX_FSR,
+				     tmp, 2);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			return ret;
+		}
+
+		if (sys_get_be16(tmp) >= len) {
+			break;
+		}
+
+		if (sys_timepoint_expired(end)) {
+			return -EIO;
+		}
+
+		k_busy_wait(W6300_CMD_POLL_US);
+	}
+
 	ret = w6300_spi_read(dev, W6300_BSB_SOCK(0), W6300_Sn_TX_WR, tmp, 2);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		return ret;
